hing (drift) and\"\n    - paragraph \"updating everything at once (an unattributable breakage). This round did neither. Here is the shape of it.\"\n    - heading \"The policy did the first half of the work\" level=2\n      - paragraph \"The policy did the first half of the work\"\n    - paragraph \"Unown's update rules were already written down, so the round started from constraints instead of vibes:\"\n    - paragraph \"no semver-major bumps (humans opt into majors),\"\n    - paragraph \"exact pins move as deliberate exact bumps ,\"\n    - paragraph \"the playwright trio moves in lockstep , and the vendored\"\n    - code\n      - paragraph \"pi-repo/\"\n    - paragraph \"workspace is an upstream-sync decision — frozen, not a routine bump surface.\"\n    - paragraph \"A sweep of all 28 root packages against the registry found the truth Dependabot-style updates hide:\"\n    - paragraph \"only six updates existed within policy. next 16.4.2 → 16.4.3 and eslint-config-next → 16.4.3 (LTS backports), marked 18.1.1 → 18.1.2 (CommonMark fixes), then three exact-pin bumps — eslint 10.13.0 → 10.14.0, lucide-reac\n    - heading \"Every stage got its own gate\" level=2\n      - paragraph \"Every stage got its own gate\"\n    - paragraph \"The updates landed in four stages, and after\"\n    - paragraph \"each one: typecheck, lint, the 2063-test unit suite, a production build, the 15-test e2e lane, and a\"\n    - code\n      - paragraph \"bun audit --prod\"\n    - paragraph \"pass. A regression that appears after stage four is a regression you can name. The engine suite (5326 tests) and the bridge suite (243) never re-ran against the updates — not out of laziness, but beca…\"\n    - code\n      - paragraph \"pi-repo/\"\n    - paragraph \"manifest or lockfile: their dependency graph\"\n    - paragraph \"cannot move. Knowing what a change cannot affect is half of verification.\"\n    - paragraph \"Mark got the sharpest gate: it renders every blog post, so the blog data was regenerated under it —\"\n    - paragraph \"byte-identical , all 37 posts and the feed.\"\n    - heading \"The part you can't unit test: motion\" level=2\n      - paragraph \"The part you can't unit test: motion\"\n    - paragraph \"framer-motion 14.6 → 14.9 is the one update that changes what the page\"\n    - paragraph \"does , not just what it links against — 14.7 moved background-color animations to the main thread and touched\"\n    - code\n      - paragraph \"AnimatePresence\"\n    - paragraph \"positioning, and the landing page's reveals ride exactly those APIs. No unit test sees that. So the round took the only measurement that can:\"\n    - list\n      - paragraph \"The landing page's own screenshot lane shot all 22 sections — both colour schemes, plus the\"\n      - code\n        - paragraph \"prefers-reduced-motion\"\n      - paragraph \"lane — against the production build. Twice on the new tree (a noise floor), once on the old tree (rebuilt from the pre-round lockfile).\"\n      - paragraph \"A per-pixel diff compared the passes.\"\n    - paragraph \"The result:\"\n    - paragraph \"the reduced-motion lane is pixel-identical between the old and new dependency trees — three shots, zero differing pixels. 21 of 25 full shots identical; the four differing frames differ only in the live star-count and a\n    - paragraph \"One honesty note worth keeping: a VLM design reviewer — our own Agnes lane — had been briefed to hunt for motion regressions and confidently reported several, including \\\"half-finished reveals\\\"\"\n    - paragraph \"in the reduced-motion frames, where nothing animates at all . Pixels beat opinions. Brief your reviewers neutrally, then measure.\"\n    - heading \"The catch that never left the machine\" level=2\n      - paragraph \"The catch that never left the machine\"\n    - paragraph \"The round's one real regression almost shipped — and it wasn't a dependency. Folding the changelog for release regenerated the landing rail, and the new release stop's chrome pushed the page to 3,930 …\"\n    - heading \"Receipts\" level=2\n      - paragraph \"Receipts\"\n    - paragraph \"The full record — what moved, what stayed and why, every gate, the A/B numbers — lives in\"\n    - link \"the research record\" value=\"https://github.com/kanishka-namdeo/Unown/blob/main/docs/dependency-round-research.md\" [e79]\n      - paragraph \"the research record\"\n    - paragraph \"and\"\n    - link \"the session log\" value=\"https://github.com/kanishka-namdeo/Unown/blob/main/docs/dependency-round-session.md\" [e82]\n      - paragraph \"the session log\"\n    - paragraph \"; the release stop is in the\"\n    - link \"changelog\" value=\"https://github.com/kanishka-namdeo/Unown/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\" [e85]\n      - paragraph \"changelog\"\n    - paragraph \". The next round is already queued — the settings ledger's spend meter and memory-health card, each with a waiting benchmark to flip. But this one ends the way a maintenance release should: nothing on…\"\n    - paragraph \"Spotted something wrong or worth adding? The record is the repo —\"\n    - link \"open an issue\" value=\"https://github.com/kanishka-namdeo/Unown/issues\" [e89]\n      - paragraph \"open an issue\"\n    - paragraph \".\"\n    - navigation \"Post navigation\"\n      - link \"← OLDER \\\"The release that never was: re-cutting v0.0.53 from a red tag\\\"\" value=\"/blog/2026-11-01-the-release-recovery-round\" [e93]\n        - paragraph \"← older\"\n        - paragraph \"\\\"The release that never was: re-cutting v0.0.53 from a red tag\\\"\"\n    - link \"All posts\" value=\"/blog\" [e96]\n      - paragraph \"All posts\"\n- contentinfo\n  - paragraph \"unown\"\n  - paragraph \"A terminal coding agent: sessions into notes, notes into verified memory.\"\n  - paragraph \"Currently in beta.\"\n  - navigation \"Footer\"\n    - link \"GitHub\" value=\"https://github.com/kanishka-namdeo/Unown\" [e103]\n      - paragraph \"GitHub\"\n    - link \"Documentation\" value=